<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Profile xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        SOURCE OF TRUTH FOR THIS PROFILE'S LAYOUT ASSIGNMENTS ONLY. Deliberately partial: it
        carries layoutAssignments and NOTHING else (no tab visibility, no userPermissions, no
        object/field permissions). Everything else this persona needs is granted through permission
        sets - DPEG_IR_Default_Access, DPEG_App_IR, DPEG_IR_Principle_Read - which is the pattern
        this whole project uses.

        🔴 THIS FILE DOES NOT DEPLOY FROM A NORMAL SOURCE DEPLOY, AND THAT IS INTENTIONAL.
        force-app/main/default/profiles/** is excluded in .forceignore (line 28): deploying whole
        profiles produced 394 errors in this org (392 tab-visibility + 2 userLicense), because the
        source profiles reference ~14 standard tabs this org does not have. The exclusion stays.
        This file is kept as the DIFFABLE RECORD of what was applied, so the assignments are not
        invisible org-only state.

        ── HOW TO APPLY IT (measured working, 2026-08-17) ──────────────────────────────────────
        Deploy it as a METADATA-FORMAT package from OUTSIDE the package directory, so .forceignore
        (which is scoped to force-app) never applies, and profile deploys stay PARTIAL - only the
        elements present in the file are written, so nothing else on the profile is disturbed:

            <tmp>/package.xml          <- Profile member "DPEG-IR-SF-Minimum Access", version 66.0
            <tmp>/profiles/DPEG-IR-SF-Minimum Access.profile   <- a copy of this file's content
            sf project deploy start --metadata-dir <tmp> --target-org <alias>

        ⚠ THE `.profile-meta.xml` SUFFIX IS SOURCE FORMAT. In the metadata-format package above the
        file must be named `DPEG-IR-SF-Minimum Access.profile` (no -meta.xml), or the API ignores it.

        ── WHY ALL FOUR ENTRIES, NOT JUST THE INVESTOR ONE ─────────────────────────────────────
        A layoutAssignments deploy can reset assignments it does not list. Contact.Investor is the
        entry that fixes the reported bug ("One or more profiles have no page layout assigned for
        the 'Contact' Object", raised when Fiaz Hirani opened the Details tab of an Investor
        Contact), but shipping it alone risked trading that break for the same break on Broker or
        on the master default. All four are therefore declared together.

        ⚠ RETRIEVING THIS BACK IS NOT A SIMPLE ROUND TRIP. A record-type-scoped layoutAssignment is
        only returned by the Metadata API when the RECORD TYPE'S OWN OBJECT is also a member of the
        retrieve manifest. A manifest of Profile + Layout alone returns ONLY the un-scoped
        `Contact-Contact Layout` line and silently omits the other three - measured 2026-08-17, and
        it reads exactly like the assignments failed to deploy when they did not. Any verification
        retrieve must include `<name>CustomObject</name>` members for Contact and Lead.
    -->
    <layoutAssignments>
        <layout>Contact-Investor Layout</layout>
        <recordType>Contact.Investor</recordType>
    </layoutAssignments>
    <layoutAssignments>
        <layout>Contact-Contact Layout</layout>
        <recordType>Contact.Broker</recordType>
    </layoutAssignments>
    <layoutAssignments>
        <layout>Contact-Contact Layout</layout>
    </layoutAssignments>
    <layoutAssignments>
        <layout>Lead-Investor Onboarding Layout</layout>
        <recordType>Lead.Investor_Onboarding</recordType>
    </layoutAssignments>
    <!--
        ⚠ ADDED (Account/Contact junction change, 2026-08-20) - the Account "Investing Entity"
        record-type-scoped layout. Same deploy mechanics as every entry above: this file is
        diffable documentation only (profiles/** is .forceignore'd); applying it requires the
        metadata-format partial-profile deploy documented at the top of this file. Retrieving this
        back also requires a CustomObject member for Account in the manifest, per the same
        measured finding documented above for Contact/Lead.
    -->
    <layoutAssignments>
        <layout>Account-Investing Entity Layout</layout>
        <recordType>Account.Investing_Entity</recordType>
    </layoutAssignments>
    <!--
        ⚠ REWORKED 2026-08-20 - NO recordType element, DELIBERATELY. AccountContactRelation cannot
        have a custom Record Type on this org (measured deploy-validation rejection - see the
        comment in layouts/AccountContactRelation-Investor-Investing Entity Layout.layout-meta.xml),
        so there is no `AccountContactRelation.<RecordType>` key to scope this assignment to. The
        reference pattern for "default/master layout for this profile+object, no record type" is
        already present in THIS SAME FILE - see the un-scoped `Contact-Contact Layout` entry above
        (no <recordType> child), which is the master default layout assignment for Contact under
        this profile. This entry mirrors that shape: it makes the reworked layout the default
        layout AccountContactRelation records use under this profile, since there is no record
        type to key a more specific assignment to.
    -->
    <layoutAssignments>
        <layout>AccountContactRelation-Investor-Investing Entity Layout</layout>
    </layoutAssignments>
</Profile>
